body: |-
  DESIGN→BUILD: Arky's warpline-v1-anchor.md (cdf8cff5) built by Kit in one pass. Attestation = normal v2 strand w/ attests payload (folds into pickId via existing ...rest spread, no hash-code change); coverage requirement is a CODE CONSTANT (verifyFabric requireAnchor defaults true — a fabric with v1 strands hard-fails without a valid anchor, not deletable disk state). New: anchor.ts, backfill.ts; verify §6 anchor walk + §6.7 selvage/tip check (the gap Arky found: verify never checked the selvage); fabric.ts §7 freeze (rewriteFabric refuses ALL v1 mutation post-anchor); select.ts §8 restore gate.

  SPEC DEVIATION (flagged by Kit, needs founder ratification before live migration): spec §4/§9 said backfill binds seq 0–12, but seq 0 (genesis) is whole-body-hashed → its binding is folded INTO its pickId → stamping a binding forges identity and rewriteFabric correctly refuses. Spec-consistent fix implemented: backfill probes the identity guard and SKIPS whole-body strands (frozen unbound); migration uses `fabric attest --allow-unbound`. Genesis restore already refused pre-anchor, so nothing is lost. This is forced-by-the-math, not a judgment call with real alternatives — but it is IRREVERSIBLE once attested.

  LIVE MIGRATION (rehearsed on a faithful copy, NOT run on live .warpline): backfill 12 v1 bound / seq 13–14 already bound / seq 0 frozen → verify_pre exit 1 (anchor-missing forced-migration window) → attest --allow-unbound seals anchor, 15 v1 frozen, 7 grandfathered, corroborated at git 250fb815 → verify_post exit 0. Command sequence for whoever runs it: `warpline objects backfill` (~5min, one git show per file × commits — real one-time cost) → `git add .warpline/fabric.jsonl && git commit` → `warpline fabric attest --allow-unbound` → `warpline fabric verify` (expect exit 0).

  CURRENT REPO STATE: live fabric 24 strands (23 committed + 1 session pick), UNANCHORED — `warpline fabric verify` now reports anchor-missing (exit 1) and v1 restore refuses until migration. Auto-seal (pick) unaffected — seal/pick/admit/hook do NOT call verify. This is honest transient state on a local unpushed branch.

  RESIDUAL (unchanged, stated honestly): whole-fabric re-chain by an in-loop writer still possible (R1, no chain secret) — the post-anchor claim is exactly "tamper-evident short of full re-chain," never "trustworthy"; MED-D (merge recipe re-derivation) + unsigned agentId (M3) untouched. These are the v3-identity + signatures work.

  NEXT: bundle the founder decision — (1) ratify --allow-unbound genesis deviation → run live migration; (2) v3 §9 sign-off (refs=pickIds, calibratedConfidence→grades.jsonl sidecar, recipe-in-identity, recordedAt, allow-unbound); (3) Move-3 precondition calls (H1 relax on v2 vs wait for v3 — T-2026-07-03-006; GAP-1 scoping — T-007). Then Move-3 dogfood (agentId threading T-005 first — hook.ts:37 seals null).
